//? Title: Verhoeff: actual D5 transitions and error detection
//? Subtitle: Actual native state and retained original experiments
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A decimal identifier can carry one check digit to detect common transcription
errors. Verhoeff uses a noncommutative group accumulator and position-dependent
permutations to catch single substitutions and unequal adjacent swaps.
)

\toc

> The method

Read digits from right to left. Permute each digit by a position table p, then
update group state c←d[c][p_i(digit)] in the dihedral group D5. Payload
generation uses permutation offset1 and appends the inverse of the final state;
validation uses offset0 and accepts residue0. The extra appended digit occupies
position0, shifting every payload permutation by one. This proves generation and
validation agree. Exhaustive mutation checks below exercise the claimed error
classes on the actual generated identifier.

> Simple worked example

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/verhoeff_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <bit>
#include <datamunge/random/quality.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/verhoeff.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto r = a::verhoeff_trace("236");
    std::print("| right offset | digit | permuted | before | after |\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n");
    for (auto q : r.steps)
        std::print("|{}|{}|{}|{}|{}|\n", q.position, q.digit, q.permuted,
                   q.before, q.after);
    std::print("\nActual check digit {}; 2363 valid {}.\n", r.check_digit,
               a::verhoeff_validate("2363"));
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Payload236, processed6,3,2");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("Actual residue {}", r.residue));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Inverse gives digit {}", r.check_digit));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/verhoeff_tiny.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| right offset | digit | permuted | before | after |
|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
|0|6|3|0|3|
|1|3|3|3|1|
|2|2|1|1|2|

Actual check digit 3; 2363 valid true.
